// Eadgar's Ruse.
//
// The only quest so far with NO cache constraint on its stage numbers: nothing in all.npc or
// all.loc carries multivar=eadgar_quest, eadgar_bits, eadgar_grain or eadgar_chickens. So the
// stages run in tens, like Mountain Daughter's.
//
// What the cache DOES dictate is the chain of objects, which spell the plan out in their own
// descriptions: Troll thistle -> "It'll be easier to grind now" -> "It's ready for mixing" ->
// Troll potion, "It's part of Eadgar's plan". And a Fake man, "It's good enough to fool a troll",
// alongside a Dirty robe and a Drunk parrot.
//
// Ops available are thinner than the object list suggests and shape the implementation:
//   eadgar_troll_thistle (npc) op1=Pick        - the thistle is an npc, not a loc
//   eadgar_zoo_keeper_aviary  op1=Talk-to      - Parroty Pete
//   eadgar_druid_washing      op1=Talk-to      - Tegid, in Taverley
//   eadgar_parrotts           NO ops           - reached with opnpcu, which needs none
//   eadgar_storeroom_guard    NO ops           - so he is a check on the door, not a conversation
//   eadgar_crate_goutweed     op1=Search
//   eadgar_storeroomdoor      op1=Open
//   eadgar_rack               op1=Search
//   eadgar_laundry_basket     op1=Search       - already shared with Mourning's End Part I
^eadgar_not_started = 0
^eadgar_started = 10
^eadgar_met_eadgar = 20
^eadgar_potion_made = 30
^eadgar_stew_dosed = 40
^eadgar_has_key = 50
^eadgar_has_goutweed = 60

// The goutweed crates sit beside the storeroom guard at abs (2856,10074) and (2857,10074); the
// guard is at (2857,10075) and the storeroom door at (2869,10085). No coord constants are needed -
// obj_find takes a single tile and no radius, so the decoy is handed to the guard rather than left
// lying near him, and the crates read %eadgar_scarecrow_items instead of scanning the floor.
